{%- from '_macros.jinja' import cmd with context -%}
{%- set lang_globs = {
  'python': '**/*.py',
  'typescript': '**/*.{ts,tsx}',
  'javascript': '**/*.{js,jsx,mjs,cjs}',
  'rust': '**/*.rs',
  'go': '**/*.go',
  'java': '**/*.java',
  'csharp': '**/*.cs',
  'cpp': '**/*.{c,cc,cpp,cxx,h,hh,hpp,cu,cuh}',
  'fortran': '**/*.{f,for,f90,f95,f03,f08,F,F90}',
  'julia': '**/*.jl',
  'other': '**/*'
} -%}
{#- Fall back to `**/*` rather than hard-failing the render if a future
    primary_language choice is added to copier.yml without a matching glob
    here. A too-broad applyTo degrades gracefully (and the note below tells
    the user to narrow it); a missing key would break generation. -#}
{%- set lang_glob = lang_globs.get(primary_language, '**/*') -%}
---
applyTo: "{{ lang_glob }}"
---
# {{ primary_language }} review rules

Path-scoped guidance for {{ primary_language }} sources, applied on top of
the repo-wide rules in `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.

- Flag exported/public functions whose error and edge-case behaviour isn't
  covered by a test.
- Flag data races in threaded / OpenMP / MPI / async code: shared mutable
  state without clear ownership or synchronization.
- Flag broad catch-alls that swallow errors without logging or rethrowing.
- Flag array/buffer indexing that can run out of bounds, and off-by-one in
  loop, grid, or halo boundaries.
- Prefer established numerical libraries over hand-rolled routines; flag
  reinvented BLAS/LAPACK, stdlib reductions, or framework array ops.

{% if lang_glob == '**/*' -%}
> `applyTo` is `**/*` because `primary_language` (`{{ primary_language }}`)
> has no language-specific glob mapped. Narrow it to your real source
> extensions (e.g. `**/*.{ext}`) so these rules only fire on code, not on
> docs or config.
{% endif -%}
> Tighten this list for {{ project_name }}: add the review rules that
> `{{ cmd('lint') }}` can't express, and delete anything it already enforces.
